  "experiment_id": "2026-09-30-e35-runner-k",
  "title": "E35: verify length decided in the model runner from the DFlash2 selector's confidence",
  "outcome": "promote",
  "outcome_detail": "Owner decision after the A-P-P-A suites. The `hybrid` policy passed the frozen held-out screen with thinking off (short tasks +5.1%, 9/10). On native Rigmark with the reference flags (reasoning effort low) code decode (+0.1%) and C1 (+1.8%) stayed within the arm A drift (+0.9%, +1.9%), prose decode was -1.5% and decode TTFT about 30 ms lower in both P suites. The owner judged the prose change to be noise and the TTFT gain real, and promoted `hybrid` as the default through a read-only policy file (the measured code bytes are unchanged).",
  "reference": {
    "operational_identity": "2026-09-30-e31-mb",
    "operational_identity_sha256": "385a68ca4451277fcf445a82cee40b8125d7f075301f99ff56d0fbfccaa2d9c1",
    "performance_baseline_id": "2026-09-30-e31-mb",
    "comparison": "same-load arm A (policy `ema`, the default's verify length with the overlay loaded)"
  },
  "candidate": {
    "change": "Wrappers of the V2 model runner's execute_model() and the DFlash2 speculator's propose(), plus the E31-MB adaptive-k scheduler with one addition. On a decode step with one request and seven scheduled drafts, tensor-parallel rank 0 chooses to verify 3 or 7 drafts from the selector's per-position confidence (isotonic survival calibration, 58/81 ms step costs), broadcasts the choice over the tensor-parallel CPU group, and every rank runs a trimmed copy of the scheduler output; trimmed drafts count as rejected. A flag file selects `ema` (no trim), `lag1` (previous draft, no wait) or `hybrid` (waits for the current draft when the rule's margin is below 0.005). Under `lag1`/`hybrid` the scheduler schedules seven drafts for single-request steps.",
    "source_sha256": {
      "scripts/node/experiments/e03/e35-runner-k/model_runner.py": "4aa67bc0379d1e39649b7eb5297f247eaa0ad7597ed087e876dc81a4075e2e36",
